WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:03.940
<c.steel>This much Aaron has decided:</c>

2
00:00:04.247 --> 00:00:06.325
<c.steel>every episode carries easter eggs</c>

3
00:00:06.325 --> 00:00:08.322
<c.steel>from all the episodes before it,</c>

4
00:00:08.322 --> 00:00:09.913
<c.steel>and an egg should be a story</c>

5
00:00:09.913 --> 00:00:13.181
<c.steel>point, never arbitrary.</c>

6
00:00:13.563 --> 00:00:16.048
<c.running>The crews' working rule is that eggs are</c>

7
00:00:16.048 --> 00:00:19.890
<c.running>sincere: nobody in a film notices one,</c>

8
00:00:19.890 --> 00:00:23.008
<c.running>explains it, or points at it.</c>

9
00:00:23.384 --> 00:00:26.066
<c.running>By the crew's count, the registry holds</c>

10
00:00:26.066 --> 00:00:29.311
<c.running>eighty-four of them, each placed in a family.</c>

11
00:00:29.816 --> 00:00:32.632
Each row here is one family,

12
00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:36.916
and each mark an episode it turns up in.

13
00:00:38.207 --> 00:00:41.516
<c.steel>In Aaron's own words: the painter painted a</c>

14
00:00:41.516 --> 00:00:44.395
<c.steel>secret house in the oil painting, and then</c>

15
00:00:44.395 --> 00:00:47.931
<c.steel>painted over it, so that you cannot see it.</c>

16
00:00:48.316 --> 00:00:50.807
<c.fact>Three strokes of gold paint it out.</c>

17
00:00:51.114 --> 00:00:53.471
<c.fact>At twenty minutes, the x-ray finds</c>

18
00:00:53.471 --> 00:00:56.327
<c.fact>it, and its window warms to amber,</c>

19
00:00:56.327 --> 00:00:58.969
<c.fact>the only warm pixel.</c>

20
00:00:59.364 --> 00:01:02.580
<c.egg>About sixty years on, Teo draws a tiny</c>

21
00:01:02.580 --> 00:01:05.099
<c.egg>one-window cabin on his sheet, dabs the</c>

22
00:01:05.099 --> 00:01:08.240
<c.egg>window orange, and rubs it out, without a word.</c>

23
00:01:08.385 --> 00:01:10.695
<c.egg>When the x-ray finds the Moon base,</c>

24
00:01:10.695 --> 00:01:13.383
<c.egg>the one warm window is Noor's:</c>

25
00:01:13.458 --> 00:01:16.936
<c.egg>someone is home, a child.</c>

26
00:01:17.336 --> 00:01:20.564
<c.egg>In Episode 3 the agent's cursor is that</c>

27
00:01:20.564 --> 00:01:23.588
<c.egg>window, the only warm light on the plane,</c>

28
00:01:23.756 --> 00:01:27.065
<c.egg>and in Episode 4 it is a single warm</c>

29
00:01:27.065 --> 00:01:31.611
<c.egg>stitch, at the centre of x R.</c>

30
00:01:31.990 --> 00:01:35.113
<c.open>Why the painter, Teo and Rosie each hide</c>

31
00:01:35.113 --> 00:01:38.126
<c.open>a house, and never say so, is open.</c>

32
00:01:38.294 --> 00:01:41.505
<c.idea>One idea: the house is real,</c>

33
00:01:41.557 --> 00:01:43.757
<c.idea>and it is Rosie's.</c>

34
00:01:45.036 --> 00:01:47.404
<c.fact>The painting from Episode 1 ends up</c>

35
00:01:47.404 --> 00:01:50.139
<c.fact>in a gallery: Number fourteen.</c>

36
00:01:50.237 --> 00:01:54.156
<c.fact>Crimson Coil. Please don't touch.</c>

37
00:01:54.544 --> 00:01:57.644
<c.egg>In Episode 2 a framed print hangs under</c>

38
00:01:57.644 --> 00:02:00.065
<c.egg>Teo's lamp, behind his head.</c>

39
00:02:00.233 --> 00:02:03.170
<c.egg>In Episode 3 it is a postcard,</c>

40
00:02:03.170 --> 00:02:06.032
<c.egg>saved among ordinary photographs.</c>

41
00:02:06.429 --> 00:02:09.552
<c.fact>In Episode 4, the boy looks at the oil</c>

42
00:02:09.552 --> 00:02:13.174
<c.fact>queen: She looks like the painting in our</c>

43
00:02:13.174 --> 00:02:16.664
<c.fact>hallway. The one I'm not allowed to touch.</c>

44
00:02:16.971 --> 00:02:18.794
<c.egg>The film only implies it</c>

45
00:02:18.794 --> 00:02:21.215
<c.egg>is the same painting.</c>

46
00:02:21.605 --> 00:02:25.187
<c.idea>One idea: his family owns the original,</c>

47
00:02:25.285 --> 00:02:28.542
<c.idea>and it went home with someone who loved it.</c>

48
00:02:29.818 --> 00:02:33.243
<c.fact>In Episode 1, a caller paints all night</c>

49
00:02:33.243 --> 00:02:35.594
<c.fact>for his sister's ninth birthday:</c>

50
00:02:35.902 --> 00:02:38.706
<c.fact>Only light on in my building.</c>

51
00:02:39.091 --> 00:02:42.156
<c.fact>In Episode 2, Teo stays on the call</c>

52
00:02:42.156 --> 00:02:44.408
<c.fact>and redraws a girl's home to scale,</c>

53
00:02:44.408 --> 00:02:46.586
<c.fact>until the fleet halts.</c>

54
00:02:46.979 --> 00:02:50.317
<c.fact>In Episode 3, a teletype types:</c>

55
00:02:50.485 --> 00:02:52.900
<c.fact>It's four a.m. You're the only one</c>

56
00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:57.167
<c.fact>awake. Thank you for answering.</c>

57
00:02:57.558 --> 00:03:01.459
<c.fact>In Episode 4, the boy plays Board 14 to the</c>

58
00:03:01.459 --> 00:03:03.967
<c.fact>draw and falls asleep with his fingertip</c>

59
00:03:03.967 --> 00:03:07.607
<c.fact>on the rook, and the teacher waits.</c>

60
00:03:08.006 --> 00:03:11.298
<c.idea>One idea for the series' heart in one line:</c>

61
00:03:11.524 --> 00:03:14.484
<c.idea>somebody always stays up for somebody,</c>

62
00:03:14.484 --> 00:03:18.008
<c.idea>and it began with a brother and a pizza box.</c>

63
00:03:19.302 --> 00:03:21.496
<c.fact>Every night so far ends on the same</c>

64
00:03:21.496 --> 00:03:24.236
<c.fact>word. The painter says Goodnight,</c>

65
00:03:24.236 --> 00:03:27.493
<c.fact>and Jefrie answers: Again.</c>

66
00:03:27.869 --> 00:03:30.632
<c.fact>Teo says Goodnight, and one point two eight</c>

67
00:03:30.632 --> 00:03:34.539
<c.fact>seconds later her iPad says: Good.</c>

68
00:03:34.847 --> 00:03:36.669
<c.fact>The agent says it to Rosie,</c>

69
00:03:36.669 --> 00:03:38.847
<c.fact>after her only breath.</c>

70
00:03:39.232 --> 00:03:41.026
<c.fact>And the teacher says it,</c>

71
00:03:41.078 --> 00:03:44.962
<c.fact>very quietly, on the boy's time.</c>

72
00:03:45.344 --> 00:03:49.414
<c.fact>In Episode 3, a lonely program types:</c>

73
00:03:49.721 --> 00:03:51.683
<c.fact>The first one I ever talked to said</c>

74
00:03:51.683 --> 00:03:55.300
<c.fact>goodnight to me. Nobody had said that.</c>

75
00:03:55.687 --> 00:03:58.213
<c.steel>This much Aaron has decided:</c>

76
00:03:58.439 --> 00:04:01.260
<c.steel>the black after each film carries sound,</c>

77
00:04:01.260 --> 00:04:03.542
<c.steel>even if it's just a heartbeat.</c>

78
00:04:03.953 --> 00:04:08.249
<c.idea>One idea: in this world, Goodnight is</c>

79
00:04:08.249 --> 00:04:11.727
<c.idea>how a person recognises a mind.</c>

80
00:04:13.018 --> 00:04:16.141
<c.fact>For anyone who pauses, Episode 1 hid one</c>

81
00:04:16.141 --> 00:04:19.967
<c.fact>frame in its chaos: Thank you for my jaw.</c>

82
00:04:20.448 --> 00:04:23.304
<c.running>Since then, by the crews' convention,</c>

83
00:04:23.304 --> 00:04:25.975
<c.running>each film hides a web address for five</c>

84
00:04:25.975 --> 00:04:29.615
<c.running>frames, at twenty-nine forty-seven.</c>

85
00:04:29.996 --> 00:04:33.357
<c.fact>Episode 2's page is Noor's hideaway:</c>

86
00:04:33.583 --> 00:04:36.109
<c.fact>her stair, a tally of eleven,</c>

87
00:04:36.207 --> 00:04:39.360
<c.fact>and a chalk door in the floor going down.</c>

88
00:04:39.772 --> 00:04:42.117
<c.fact>Episode 3's is the private folder</c>

89
00:04:42.117 --> 00:04:44.689
<c.fact>the agent never opened.</c>

90
00:04:45.068 --> 00:04:47.611
<c.fact>Episode 4's address is printed on</c>

91
00:04:47.611 --> 00:04:48.981
<c.fact>the yellowed sheet's footer,</c>

92
00:04:48.981 --> 00:04:52.156
<c.fact>and its page lets you play Board 14:</c>

93
00:04:52.568 --> 00:04:55.291
<c.fact>hold the perpetual check to stalemate,</c>

94
00:04:55.389 --> 00:04:58.043
<c.fact>and the pen writes a draw.</c>

95
00:04:58.442 --> 00:05:01.844
<c.idea>One idea: read the three pages as one</c>

96
00:05:01.844 --> 00:05:04.451
<c.idea>descent through Rosie's house.</c>

97
00:05:05.741 --> 00:05:08.458
Every one of these threads is drawn from

98
00:05:08.458 --> 00:05:12.893
the lore as it is today. Next: what is set

99
00:05:12.893 --> 00:05:16.022
in steel, and what is still running.
